+
+Goal: after the large scale kernels, improve the actual algorithms used inside them while preserving Minecraft/Paper semantics.
+
+Implemented in this slice:
+
+1. EWMA/derivative tick control law for invisible work budgets.
+2. Player-motion-aware lookahead for chunk planning and entity candidate preparation.
+3. Stable entity spatial banding for read-only tracker candidate scans.
+4. Lossless network delta/shape planning for repeated packet fanout without packet drops or stream reordering.
+5. A hard-coded Minecraft logic phase DAG: read-only prepare can be concurrent, but redstone/block entity/entity tick/plugin event/commit phases stay ordered.
+6. Conservative plugin semantic classifier for read-only/pure compute versus Bukkit-visible ordered commit.
+
+Next step: wire these algorithms deeper into concrete tracker, chunk-send, packet-encoding and plugin scheduler hot paths after local JDK 25 Gradle validation.
